From e95f46e4c0e86d36c5c195e5707c4c649c90c955 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 08:51:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: pmdomain: Store cached power-down state index
 as an unsigned int

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

genpd caches the state index selected by the governor so the next
power-down decision can reuse it while constraints remain unchanged.

The cache currently stores the index in a bool, truncating every index
above 1. Use unsigned int to match generic_pm_domain.state_idx and preserve
the complete selected index. Domains that only select state 0 or 1 are
unchanged.

Fixes: e94999688e3a ("PM / Domains: Add genpd governor for CPUs")
Signed-off-by: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Assisted-by: OpenAI-Codex:gpt-5.6
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
---
 include/linux/pm_domain.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/pm_domain.h b/include/linux/pm_domain.h
index f925614aeb..103e74486e 100644
--- a/include/linux/pm_domain.h
+++ b/include/linux/pm_domain.h
@@ -171,7 +171,7 @@ struct genpd_governor_data {
 	ktime_t last_enter;
 	bool reflect_residency;
 	bool cached_power_down_ok;
-	bool cached_power_down_state_idx;
+	unsigned int cached_power_down_state_idx;
 };
 
 struct genpd_power_state {
From f2f87aa6aa27401510455298e9fcbea2df78bc35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 21:36:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: sched: idle: Treat wakeup no-constraint as
 unbounded

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

The CPU wakeup latency QoS no-constraint value is a sentinel, not a finite
latency budget.  When entering s2idle, use U64_MAX for cpuidle state
selection if no CPU wakeup latency constraint is active.

This preserves finite constraints while avoiding rejection of states with
firmware-provided latency values larger than S32_MAX usec.

Signed-off-by: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Assisted-by: OpenAI-Codex:gpt-5.6
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
---
 kernel/sched/idle.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/idle.c b/kernel/sched/idle.c
index 052435f4d3..056245ae17 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/idle.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/idle.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
  *        tasks which are handled in sched/fair.c )
  */
 #include <linux/cpuidle.h>
+#include <linux/pm_qos.h>
 #include <linux/suspend.h>
 #include <linux/livepatch.h>
 #include "sched.h"
@@ -214,8 +215,14 @@ static void cpuidle_idle_call(bool stop_tick)
 		u64 max_latency_ns;
 
 		if (idle_should_enter_s2idle()) {
-			max_latency_ns = cpu_wakeup_latency_qos_limit() *
-					 NSEC_PER_USEC;
+			s32 latency_limit_us = cpu_wakeup_latency_qos_limit();
+
+			if (latency_limit_us ==
+			    PM_QOS_RESUME_LATENCY_NO_CONSTRAINT)
+				max_latency_ns = U64_MAX;
+			else
+				max_latency_ns = (u64)latency_limit_us *
+						 NSEC_PER_USEC;
 
 			entered_state = call_cpuidle_s2idle(drv, dev,
 							    max_latency_ns);
From b6667ee782222e44e85d9f3f662d3bc9900d4852 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:48:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: pmdomain: Treat unconstrained CPU wake latency
 as unlimited

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

cpu_system_power_down_ok() converts the CPU resume-latency QoS value to
nanoseconds before comparing it with genpd state latency. However,
PM_QOS_RESUME_LATENCY_NO_CONSTRAINT is a sentinel rather than a finite
microsecond limit. Treating it as an ordinary value can reject a valid
state whose combined latency is larger than the converted sentinel.

Detect the sentinel before conversion and allow any state latency when no
constraint is present. Continue enforcing zero and finite latency requests
normally.

Fixes: 8e7de6dc4209 ("pmdomain: Respect the CPU system wakeup QoS limit for s2idle")
Signed-off-by: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Assisted-by: OpenAI-Codex:gpt-5.6
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/governor.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/governor.c b/drivers/pmdomain/governor.c
index 96737abbb4..fc86190ca8 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/governor.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/governor.c
@@ -427,8 +427,10 @@ static bool cpu_power_down_ok(struct dev_pm_domain *pd)
 
 static bool cpu_system_power_down_ok(struct dev_pm_domain *pd)
 {
-	s64 constraint_ns = cpu_wakeup_latency_qos_limit() * NSEC_PER_USEC;
 	struct generic_pm_domain *genpd = pd_to_genpd(pd);
+	s32 constraint_us = cpu_wakeup_latency_qos_limit();
+	bool no_constraint;
+	s64 constraint_ns;
 	int state_idx = genpd->state_count - 1;
 
 	if (!(genpd->flags & GENPD_FLAG_CPU_DOMAIN)) {
@@ -436,12 +438,17 @@ static bool cpu_system_power_down_ok(struct dev_pm_domain *pd)
 		return true;
 	}
 
+	no_constraint = constraint_us == PM_QOS_RESUME_LATENCY_NO_CONSTRAINT;
+	constraint_ns = no_constraint ? PM_QOS_RESUME_LATENCY_NO_CONSTRAINT_NS :
+			(s64)constraint_us * NSEC_PER_USEC;
+
 	/* Find the deepest state for the latency constraint. */
 	while (state_idx >= 0) {
 		s64 latency_ns = genpd->states[state_idx].power_off_latency_ns +
 				 genpd->states[state_idx].power_on_latency_ns;
 
-		if (latency_ns <= constraint_ns) {
+		/* The no-constraint value is a sentinel, not a latency budget. */
+		if (no_constraint || latency_ns <= constraint_ns) {
 			genpd->state_idx = state_idx;
 			return true;
 		}
From e67b10d0eb72bb9885b8b6d953c12b7db7e31ec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 21:11:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: pmdomain: Correct rejected idle-state
 accounting

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

pm_genpd_inc_rejected() accepts the state index whose asynchronous
power-off attempt failed, but updates the domain current state index
instead. The current index may have changed before the correction runs,
causing the wrong usage and rejected counters to be adjusted.

The helper also leaves usage_s2idle incremented when a suspend-to-idle
entry fails. Accept the entry context from callers, use the supplied index,
and undo the s2idle counter when genpd incremented it. Reject an
out-of-range index before accessing the state table.

Fixes: 9861f21ff16b ("pmdomain: core: Add genpd helper to correct the usage/rejected counters")
Signed-off-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Assisted-by: OpenAI-Codex:gpt-5.6
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
