From cc2be96ae537fdd0eb6211a0fa3065b5e1444e61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:04:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: pmdomain: Distinguish s2idle state usage

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

Synchronous genpd power-off is used for more than suspend-to-idle.
System-sleep and PREEMPT_RT CPU-hotplug paths also use
dev_pm_genpd_suspend(), so inferring the accounting context from the
presence of a system_power_down_ok() callback classifies those transitions
as s2idle.

Add an explicit s2idle variant of the suspend helper and propagate that
context through synchronous parent power-off. Keep the existing helper as
the non-s2idle path, update the PSCI and RISC-V SBI s2idle callers, and use
the same explicit context when correcting a rejected selection.

Co-developed-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Assisted-by: OpenAI-Codex:gpt-5.6
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c      |  2 +-
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-riscv-sbi.c |  2 +-
 drivers/pmdomain/core.c             | 41 ++++++++++++++++++-----------
 include/linux/pm_domain.h           |  2 ++
 4 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
index 009bbedcd9..1562a5b09d 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@ static __cpuidle int __psci_enter_domain_idle_state(struct cpuidle_device *dev,
 
 	/* Do runtime PM to manage a hierarchical CPU toplogy. */
 	if (s2idle)
-		dev_pm_genpd_suspend(pd_dev);
+		dev_pm_genpd_suspend_s2idle(pd_dev);
 	else
 		pm_runtime_put_sync_suspend(pd_dev);
 
