From 5231c8fe672a6e8e7cde1b6cced64c2ba5917c14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:05:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: cpuidle: psci: Correct rejected states for the
 full domain path

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

Each successful genpd power-off callback replaces the single per-CPU PSCI
domain-state record. In a multilevel topology, firmware rejection can
therefore correct the usage and rejected counters for only the final
selected domain.

Count the attached domain paths during CPU initialization and preallocate
enough per-CPU storage for every selection. Collect each selected domain
only while preparing a cpuidle firmware entry, use the final record for the
composite PSCI state, and correct every recorded domain if firmware rejects
it. Propagate an exhausted record array back through the genpd power-off
callback.

Keeping collection scoped to the cpuidle transaction also prevents syscore
and CPU-hotplug genpd transitions from accumulating irrelevant state.

Co-developed-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Assisted-by: OpenAI-Codex:gpt-5.6
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
